File: relaxng.c
Line: 7040
Function: xmlRelaxNGCleanupTree
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: If creating the <name> node/text fails (xmlNewChild/xmlNewDocNode/xmlNewDocText return NULL), 'text' remains NULL. When the original node has no 'ns' attribute and is an 'attribute' element, the code unconditionally calls xmlSetProp(text, ...). This dereferences a NULL 'text' pointer, leading to a crash. The path is: name = xmlGetProp(...) succeeds; node creation fails → text == NULL; ns == NULL; cur->name == 'attribute' → xmlSetProp(text, ...).

